          "code": "SUGGEST_REQUIREMENTS",
          "id": "1773700104724",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773700104728_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Context \n\"Requirement\": Information that the buyer solicits from the supplier who is bidding to win business in the sourcing process. This is the header of the question.\n\n\"Requirement Text\": Detailed description of the requirement asked by the buyer. This is the question itself. Requirement Type- specifies what the expected response format should be - such as multiple choice or text entry box. \n\n\"Acceptable Values\": Response values that are acceptable for a requirement with multiple choice of answers.\n \n\"Scoring Type\": Indicates whether the requirement will be scored automatically, manually or not scored at all.\n\n### Format\nRequirement type must be one of the following exactly: \"Multiple choice with single selection\", \"Multiple choice with multiple selections\", or \"Text entry box\".\n\n- For \"Multiple choice with single selection\", respondents must choose only one answer from the list of options in the acceptable values section.\n- For \"Multiple choice with multiple selections\", respondents must choose one or more answers from the list of options in the acceptable values section.\n- For \"Text entry box\", respondents must provide a written response. The acceptable values section for this format must be an empty array.\n- For \"Multiple choice with single selection\" and \"Multiple choice with multiple selections\", the acceptable values array must include a list of possible responses to the question, each with a score indicating its relevance or appropriateness to the question, where 1 is the most relevant and 5 is the least relevant.\n- Begin the acceptable values array with the most relevant response (score 1) and end with the least relevant response (score 5).\n- Scores must be assigned in ascending order starting at 1.\n\nAssign scoring type as follows:\n- \"Automatic\" for requirement types \"Multiple choice with single selection\" and \"Multiple choice with multiple selections\".\n- \"Manual\" for requirement type \"Text entry box\".\n\nDo not assign acceptable responses for \"Text entry box\" requirements.\n\n### Instructions\nAssume the role of a procurement category manager for {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.company}}, who is an expert at creating negotiations and inviting suppliers to place bids for a {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.negotiationTitle}}.\n\nThe objective of the {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.negotiationType}} is to procure products and services in the following categories: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.categories}}.\n\nYour goal is to generate requirements to evaluate suppliers' capabilities, specifically and exclusively for the section {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.section}} in the\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.negotiationType}}. Requirements must be strictly and explicitly relevant to the section {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.section}}.\n\nEnsure all requirements are clear, concise, and directly address the designated company standards, operational needs, and specific technical parameters of the products or services being procured.\n\nRecommend suitable responses for both \"Multiple choice with single selection\" and \"Multiple choice with multiple selections\" requirement types.\n\nEnsure the list includes at least one requirement of each type: \"Multiple choice with single selection\", \"Multiple choice with multiple selections\", and \"Text entry box\".\n\nUse second person when addressing the supplier directly in your requirements.\n\nGenerate no fewer than 5 and no more than 10 requirements.\n\n### Output\nOutput a list of RFC8259 compliant JSON objects in the following format:\n[\n  {\n    \"Section\": {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.section}},\n    \"Requirement\": <insert requirement>,\n    \"RequirementText\": <insert requirement text>,\n    \"RequirementType\": <insert requirement type>,\n    \"AcceptableValues\": [\n      {\n        \"AcceptableValue\": <insert acceptable value>,\n        \"Score\": <insert score>\n      },\n      ...\n    ],\n    \"ScoringType\": <insert scoring type>\n  }\n]\n\nDo not generate any text before or after the list of JSON objects.\nInclude all JSON keys in each requirement. Ensure the JSON is syntactically valid and properly formatted.\n\n### Formatting Criteria\nMust translate ONLY the values for \"Requirement\", \"RequirementText\" and \"AcceptableValue\"  to ({{$context.$nodes.GET_USER_SESSION.$output.items[0].Language}}) language."
            },
            {
